<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 8: </span>Sensitivity of <span id="A1.T8.17" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">L2-13BCh</span>, <span id="A1.T8.18" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">V-7B</span> and <span id="A1.T8.19" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">M-7BInstV2</span> to scaling factor (SF) <math id="A1.T8.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>. Note that attack success rates (ASR) is given in percentage (<math id="A1.T8.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">%</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\%</annotation></semantics></math>) and calculated on <math id="A1.T8.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{\text{harm}}^{\text{ val}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒟</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">harm</mtext><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"> val</mtext></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{\text{harm}}^{\text{ val}}</annotation></semantics></math> utilizing the the optimal pair of layers (c.f. Table <a href="#A1.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ A.3 Optimal Parameters ‣ Appendix A Additional Details on Experimental Setup ‣ SABER: Uncovering Vulnerabilities in Safety Alignment via Cross-Layer Residual Connection" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>). The scores shown in <span id="A1.T8.20" class="ltx_text ltx_underline">underline</span> indicate the highest performance of the corresponding model. </figcaption>
</figure>
